 42 loose ones become four tens, with two ones left. Add those four tens to the original six tens. Now Lena has ten tens and two ones. Exchange the ten tens for one hundred. The number of counters has not changed; only the units used to describe them have changed.</p><figure id=\"place-value-after\" class=\"model k-story-source-model\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 300 140\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"place-value-after-title\"><title id=\"place-value-after-title\">1 hundred, 0 tens, and 2 ones; 102 units altogether</title><g data-hundred=\"100\"><rect data-unit=\"hundred-cell\" x=\"8\" y=\"20\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#166d5e\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect data-unit=\"hundred-cell\" x=\"18\" y=\"20\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#166d5e\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect data-unit=\"hundred-cell\" x=\"28\" y=\"20\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#166d5e\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect data-unit=\"hundred-cell\" x=\"38\" y=\"20\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#166d5e\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect data-unit=\"hundred-cell\" x=\"48\" y=\"20\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#166d5e\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect data-unit=\"hundred-cell\" x=\"58\" y=\"20\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#166d5e\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect data-unit=\"hundred-cell\" x=\"68\" y=\"20\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#166d5e\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect data-unit=\"hundred-cell\" x=\"78\" y=\"20\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#166d5e\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect data-unit=\"hundred-cell\" x=\"88\" y=\"20\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#166d5e\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect data-unit=\"hundred-cell\" x=\"98\" y=\"20\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#166d5e\" stroke=\"white\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect data-unit=\"hundred-cell\" x=\"8\" y=\"30\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#166d5e\" stroke=\"white\" strok